{"from": "text:john-11-9", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-20-03-04-daylight-hours", "note": "Cross-reference: 'Aren't there twelve hours of daylight?' - the same twelve-hour daylight reckoning inside the NT."}
{"from": "text:1-kings-2-19", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-20-20-21-mother-request", "note": "Cross-reference: Bathsheba, the king's mother, sat at Solomon's right hand - the honoured seat the mother of the sons of Zebedee asks for her sons."}
{"from": "text:isaiah-51-17", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-20-22-the-cup", "note": "Cross-reference: Jerusalem 'have drunk from Yahweh's hand the cup of his wrath' - the cup as a figure for an allotted fate of suffering."}
